message: "If you use or cite this work, please use the metadata below."
title: "CIF Ancient Systems Test Series (incorporating The Giza Transmission Hypothesis)"
abstract: >-
  Eight disciplined, fully-cited case studies that stress-test the Coherent
  Inheritance Framework (CIF) against real archaeological and historical
  evidence of knowledge transmission, loss, and survival across deep time:
  the Giza pyramids, Aboriginal oral traditions, the Antikythera Mechanism,
  the Late Bronze Age Collapse, Japanese tsunami stones, Polynesian wayfinding,
  Göbekli Tepe, and undeciphered scripts. Each study is written to be
  falsifiable, separates established fact from inference and speculation, and
  ends with a shared verdict taxonomy and a mandatory falsification check. The
  series includes the framework document, a cross-disciplinary grading review,
  and a capstone synthesis. Version 2.2.0 adds Series II ("recovery systems"):
  eight further cases examining what can be recovered after a break — the
  Rosetta Stone, Linear B, Roman concrete, ancient music reconstruction,
  Wôpanâak language reclamation, the Apollo F-1 engine, the BBC Domesday
  Project, and Greek Fire — with a Series II synthesis. Series II received a
  human-directed verification pass on 2026-07-29.
